System information\n\nGodot v4.8.dev (e2b424692) - Fedora Linux 44 (KDE Plasma Desktop Edition) on X11 - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor (3840x2160 @ 240.02 Hz) - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5090 (nvidia; 615.71.09) - AMD Ryzen 9 9950X3D 16-Core Processor (32 threads) - 62.33 GiB memory - PulseAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\n### Issue description\n\nTrail3D has normals oriented in the wrong direction. This means that to perform backface culling, you actually need to use `cull_front` in the custom shader rather than `cull_back`.\n\nExpected appearance with `cull_back` | Current appearance with `cull_back`\n-|-\n<img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/41ce605b-81bb-49db-a1ee-0b14abf73a0b\" /> | <img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/ece61b84-cecc-4ef3-b10f-e814cbe77804\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n- Add a Trail3D node with the Billboard mode (the default).\n- Set a translucent color for the trail (alpha < 1.0).\n- Set the material mode to Custom, and replace `cull_disabled` with `cull_back`.\n- Notice the trail (mostly) disappearing.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[test_trail_cull.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/32617164/test_trail_cull.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users